title: Payers › History & Changes › Suggestions from Historian
route: /payers/summit?tab=history
intro: Historian reads how the payer ruled over the last 90 days and suggests changes to the process. 'Re-learn from decisions' waits about three seconds, then proposes at most one change at a time. A suggestion is never applied on its own: a person accepts or dismisses it. An accepted suggestion adds its branch to the earlier process view (the record the migrated workflow was made from) and to a DRAFT of the migrated workflow in the Workflow Builder, and is written to the edit audit; the published workflow does not change until a person publishes the draft. The card says so. If the graph has no place for the branch, only the earlier view gets it. A dismissed suggestion is not offered again.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open History & Changes\nthe section 'Suggestions from Historian'\nopens by itself when a suggestion waits"
screen sm "Closed: 'None waiting. Re-learn from decisions to ask for one.'\nor 'N waiting for you. Nothing changes unless you accept.'"
screen top "Open: 'Re-learn from decisions' and one line\n'Historian reads how Summit ruled over the last 90 days and suggests a change to the process.'"
click rl "Click 'Re-learn from decisions'"
process sp "Button spins\nA line 'Historian is reviewing how Summit ruled over the last 90 days.'"
agent hs "Historian reads the last 90 days\n(demo: about 3 seconds, scripted)"
decision lv "Still on Payers after 3 seconds?"
endx drop "Result dropped"
decision dn "Is there a suggestion that is not on the process yet\nand was not dismissed?"
toast t0 "'Nothing new to propose'\n'The workflow already matches how Summit ruled in the last 90 days.'"
toast t1 "'Historian has a suggestion'\n'Review it here. The workflow has not changed.'"
screen pc "One card per suggestion\nHistorian chip, 'Suggestion: Ask for a therapy note on continued stays'\nWhy (6 of Summit's last 9 information requests)\n'Under Gather the documents: If request is a continued-stay request → File step. Add a therapy note...'\n'Accept proposal', 'Dismiss'\n'Applies to the earlier process view and to a draft of the migrated workflow\nin the Workflow Builder. Historian never changes a workflow on its own.'"
process bd "The History & Changes tab badge counts waiting suggestions"
click ac "Click 'Accept proposal'"
store ap "The branch is added to the earlier process view (version goes up by one)\n'Edits waiting' goes up by one"
store dr "The same branch is added to a DRAFT of the migrated workflow\none more condition in the step's decision and one more step it leads to\nThe published version keeps matching new cases until the draft is published"
store lg "Edit audit: 'Workflow' line\n'Accepted Historian's proposal: ...'\n'Added a branch under Gather the documents'"
store nt "Bell notification 'Summit workflow edited'"
toast ta "'Proposal accepted'\n'Added under Gather the documents to the earlier process view (version 8)\nand to a draft of the migrated workflow. Publish the draft in the Workflow Builder to use it.'"
click di "Click 'Dismiss'"
store ds "Suggestion removed; its title is remembered\nso Historian does not offer it again"
toast td "'Proposal dismissed'\n'The workflow did not change.'"
process nw "Dismiss changes nothing in any workflow\nA published workflow only changes when a person publishes a draft"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Earlier process view"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Edit audit"
goto g4 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Save a draft and publish"
end e1 "A person decided; nothing changed on its own"

s1 --> sm --> top --> rl --> sp --> hs --> lv
lv -->|No| drop
lv -->|Yes| dn
dn -->|No| t0 --> e1
dn -->|Yes| t1 --> pc --> bd
pc --> ac --> ap --> dr --> lg --> nt --> ta --> e1
pc --> di --> ds --> td --> nw --> e1
ap -.-> g1
ap -.-> g2
lg -.-> g3
dr -.-> g4
